----------------------------------------- Signal Forms ---------------------------------------

- LET'S MIGRATE TO SIGNAL FORMS!

- Angular v22 introduced a new way to handle forms using signals. Let’s refactor our login
    form to use this new approach!


1️⃣ In Login, change the form declaration to use form(). Update the validation logic to use
    signal-based validators and to have the same validation rules as before.


2️⃣ Then update the submit logic to use the submission.action option of signal-based forms. ⚠️The
    submission callback should call an async component method instead of subscribing to the
    Observable directly: import firstValueFrom from rxjs, await the service call with
    firstValueFrom(…​), and wrap the submission logic in a try/catch block so the failure signal is
    still updated on error while successful submissions still navigate to the home page.

        private async submit() {
            this.failureSignal.set(false);
            const { ... } = this.form().value();
            try {
                await firstValueFrom(this.userService....);
                await this.router.navigateByUrl('/');
            } catch {
                this.failureSignal.set(true);
            }
        }
    
    In the end everything should be imported from @angular/forms/signals instead of @angular/forms.


3️⃣ Finally, modify the template to use the FormField directive and the FormRoot directive
    ([formRoot] on <form>) and update the error display blocks.
    Signal forms have a nice customization feature: you can automatically bind CSS classes to your
    form fields based on their state! Bootstrap has a very nice support for validation, we should
    use it.
    In app.config.ts, add the following provider:

        app.config.ts
        provideSignalFormsConfig({
            classes: {
                'is-invalid': field => field.state().invalid() && field.state().touched()
            }
        })
    
    This will add the is-invalid Bootstrap CSS class to any invalid signal form field, displaying a
    red border around the field automatically 🚀.
    You can now remove the global CSS styles for invalid fields in styles.css.


4️⃣ Do not forget to copy all the test files and run ng test to be sure that everything is OK.


