🧠Remember:

⚠️ In the reactive form we build earlier as the exercise in the previous Chapter: forms, we directly
    subscribed to the Observable<UserModel> which gets returned from the method
    authenticate(login: string, password: string) in user service as:

        this.userService.authenticate(login, password).subscribe({
        next: () => this.router.navigateByUrl('/'),
        error: () => this.authenticationFailed.set(true)
        });
    
    Unlike the previous approach, here in the signal forms, the submission callback calls an
    async component method authenticate instead of subscribing to the Observable directly:

        submission: {
            action: async () => await this.authenticate() 👈
        }

        private async authenticate() {
            this.authenticationFailed.set(false);
            const { login, password } = this.credentials().value();
            try {
                await firstValueFrom(👉this.userService.authenticate(login, password));
                await this.router.navigateByUrl('/');
                return;
            } catch {
                this.authenticationFailed.set(true);
            }
        }